# Prettier ignores generated artefacts and build output.
#
# `pnpm-lock.yaml` is written by pnpm: reformatting it creates a diff on every install and
# gains nothing. `reports/` and `evals/datasets/` are produced by `evals/run.py` and
# `evals/generate_datasets.py`, so formatting them would be undone by the next run — and the
# check that matters for those files is the eval suite itself, not their line breaks.
pnpm-lock.yaml
reports/
evals/datasets/
.next/
node_modules/
coverage/
